# [M5.0] D27 axis 6 -- caseless fold: cross-block pairs, non-folds, closure,
# fold-before-negate (extract Sec 4.1-4.3). 48 blocks (see generator header for
# the count discrepancy vs the table's ~60), 4 subjects each -> 192 cases.
# Oracle: libpcre2, options=PCRE2_UTF|PCRE2_CASELESS (pcrec has no UCP axis,
# so the non-UCP column is pcrec's own promised semantics throughout).
#
# PINNED TO TODAY'S BEHAVIOUR, NOT PROMOTED TO THE ORACLE ABOVE (lane
# utfprom, [M5.0] stage 2 close, on the manager's explicit instruction):
# non-ASCII caseless folding is not implemented yet (stage 4) -- pcrec's
# `(?i)`/`flags i` under `-e utf8` does ASCII-only fold today (k<->K, a<->A,
# ..., the pre-existing VM ascii-fold form), so every "partner"/"closure"/
# "fold-before-negate" cell that needs a REAL Unicode fold (KELVIN
# SIGN<->k, LONG S<->s, etc.) does not match. 44 of 48 blocks compile (4
# stay `perr`: `[^\p{Ll}]`-bodied fold-before-negate cells still need
# module `unicode-props`, stage 3). Of the 44, 20 blocks (29 cells)
# disagree with the PCRE2_UTF|PCRE2_CASELESS oracle recorded in each
# block's own comment above -- **that oracle comment is left UNCHANGED
# for provenance**, and the LIVE case lines below it are pcrec's REAL
# observed answer today, added with `flags i` (missing from every block as
# authored -- the corpus's own future-case comments assume it). This is a
# KNOWN, pre-identified gap (stage 4), not a stage-2 finding: landing full
# Unicode case folding is "restore the oracle values from the comments
# above, drop the ASCII-fold values, re-run."

# axis6 block pair-KELVIN-lower-bare | pattern: k
#   [lower U+006B] m "k" 0 1   # oracle=PCRE2_UTF|PCRE2_CASELESS
#   [upper U+004B] m "K" 0 1   # oracle=PCRE2_UTF|PCRE2_CASELESS
#   [partner-0 U+212A] m "\xe2\x84\xaa" 0 3   # oracle=PCRE2_UTF|PCRE2_CASELESS
#   [control-x U+0078] n "x"   # oracle=PCRE2_UTF|PCRE2_CASELESS
# pcre2-only
pattern k
encoding utf8
flags i
m "k" 0 1
m "K" 0 1
n "\xe2\x84\xaa"
n "x"

